1.text:
The white regions consist of exactly four rectangular blocks inside the canton. These blocks are the Cartesian product of two disjoint horizontal row-blocks with two disjoint vertical column-blocks. Their indicator is therefore the rank-1 matrix \(uv^T\) (with \(u\) supported only on those two row-blocks and \(v\) supported only on those two column-blocks). All pixels outside the canton are uniformly red, so they contribute nothing further to the white indicator \(S\). Hence \(S\) itself has rank exactly 1 at every resolution that respects the flag geometry, \(M=aJ+(b-a)S\) has rank at most 2, and the bound is attained for generic \(a\neq b\).

The three column-type patterns cited by the rank-3 arguments are scalar multiples of one another once the shared row- and column-supports of the cross are taken into account; they therefore lie in the two-dimensional span already generated by \(J\) and \(S\). No algebraic counter-example to the factorization exists.

