2.text:
The white indicator \(W\) is supported exactly on the Cartesian product of two horizontal bands (the white row blocks above/below the horizontal arm of the cross) and two vertical bands (the white column blocks left/right of the vertical arm). This forces the algebraic identity \(W=uv^T\) for indicator vectors \(u,v\), independent of pixel resolution. Consequently \(M=aJ+(b-a)W\) is the sum of two rank-at-most-1 matrices and satisfies \(\operatorname{rank}(M)\le2\), attained for generic \(a\neq b\).

All column patterns inside the canton are scalar multiples of the single vector \(u\) once the shared supports of the cross arms are used; the three apparent signatures therefore lie in \(\operatorname{span}\{J,W\}\) and cannot raise the dimension. The same identity rules out any resolution-dependent increase.

